                <pb facs="0234" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg146"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Peking,
                                China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-02-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1503.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm your telegram
                    received February 10.</p>
                <p>The Chinese Government have readily consented, and I have sent telegraphic
                    instructions to Consul Miller to take charge of Japanese interests in his
                    jurisdiction in accordance with your instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
